A structure-awareness review found one issue before finalizing G4: because every update touches only a fixed-gap chord, an informed solver would search those \(n\) chords, not all \(\binom n2\) tournament arcs. I’m tightening the stated certificate language to those chords and resampling from \(\binom nK\); the hard-preset space remains enormous, but the reported probability will now use the honest prior.
