The honest prior exposed a real failure: the usual indegree-order heuristic recovered the planted set on 8/8 instances when the chord gap was large. I’m correcting the family rather than relabelling the attack. Using gap-2 chords creates local score ties and misorderings; a 20-seed sweep shows the indegree heuristic at 0/20 while the parity certificate remains exact. Difficulty will now scale through ambient size, decoy multiplicity, and replay length—not through the gap.
