-of involutive identities, not a search over feedback sets.
+What makes the problem easy, and the Track decision.  The Introduction says
+static FAST is NP-hard but cites a 2^{O(sqrt(K))} n^{O(1)} parameterized
+algorithm.  The paper deliberately uses the textbook 3^K branching routine;
+Theorem 3.2 gives O(3^K K log^2 n) full-model query time after O(log^2 n)
+updates.  Therefore a Track A claim would be false.  On this distribution an
+even stronger exact method computes all indegrees and selects the strictly
+descending arcs in O(n^2), then reads their matching.  It is implemented and
+measured as the Track B reference algorithm.
 
