codex
The corrected baseline is now measured at roughly 8,800 exact range/XOR operations on hard versus 184 for the structural route. I also replaced an unnecessarily quadratic verifier traversal with an exact check against the displayed initial topological order: batches can change only fixed-gap chords, so “no undeleted backward chord remains” is both necessary (each makes a directed triangle) and sufficient (all remaining arcs follow that order). This keeps verification cheap at the enlarged preset without weakening it.
